          "kind": "finished",
          "message": "## Done — a real INI parser, spec-conformant and verified\n\n`moon test` → **66/66 pass** (12 public fixtures + 54 of my own), `moon check --deny-warn` → **0 errors, 0 warnings**, `moon fmt --check` → clean, `moon info` → interfaces up to date.\n\n### What I built\n\nRoot package `tonyfettes/ini`, split by responsibility (45–118 non-comment code lines each):\n\n| file | role |\n| --- | --- |\n| `errors.mbt` | `ParseError` suberror with a message naming the construct |\n| `scanner.mbt` | code-unit scanning, blank/comment predicates, `trim_blanks`, `split_lines`, trailing-backslash run |\n| `section.mbt` | `[name]` headers: exact bracket syntax, wrap-quote stripping, blank-name rejection |\n| `value.mbt` | the three carriers, per-carrier escape decoding, inline comments, backslash continuations |\n| `parser.mbt` | line classification + document fold (last-wins, section re-open) |\n| `printer.mbt` | `print`: double-quoted values, section headers with protective quotes |\n\nKey algorithms: code-unit (UTF-16) scanning that can never mistake half a surrogate pair for syntax; continuation decided on the raw line's backslash-run parity *before* escape decoding (not invertible otherwise); the separator line cut at its inline comment *before* that parity test, so a `\\` inside a comment cannot swallow the next line; continuation lines appended verbatim (\"text, not syntax\"); folded with one map alias so re-opening a section needs no special case; printing quotes every value and adds a quote pair to section names that would otherwise lose their blanks or quotes.\n\n### Tests added\n`ini_lines_test.mbt` (lines, CR/LF/CRLF, comments, sections, entries, key validation), `ini_values_test.mbt` (all three escape tables, quoted-value errors, run table N=1..4, continuations, printing), `ini_fuzz_test.mbt` (random syntax strings + generated documents; asserts `parse` never panics and `parse(print(doc)) == doc`, and **fails if its generator degenerates**), `ini_readme_test.mbt` (the README example, kept runnable). Helper names are `edge_*`-prefixed so the withheld private test file cannot collide with them in the shared black-box test package.\n\n### Verification beyond `moon test`\nThree independent audit rounds (subagents, byte copies of the sources in a scratch project) plus ~116k exhaustive/random sandbox cases. They found and I fixed five real defects: `print` not round-tripping blank-padded section names, blank names hidden inside quotes (`[\" \"]`) being accepted, continuation lines being comment-stripped, a vacuous fuzz generator (Int32 overflow in my LCG made 3000 inputs all `\"\"`), and a trailing CR at EOF with no LF being treated as a line break. The final round reports **0 findings — conforms to `specs/ini.md`**.\n\n### Caveats\n- `moon.pkg` now imports `moonbitlang/core/test` only `for \"test\"` and turns off two *style-only* lints (`deprecated_syntax`, `test_unqualified_package`) that originate in `ini_spec.mbt`/`ini_pub_test.mbt`, which this task forbids editing; the file explains why. No correctness lint is disabled.\n- Ambiguities I resolved and documented in the README: a comment may follow a header glued to `]` (`[s]; note` accepted); quotes inside an unquoted value are ordinary characters; `print` cannot carry keys starting with `;`/`#`/`[` or blank section names — none of which `parse` can produce.\n- A leftover data file `rename_edits.json` (generated edits for the helper rename, already applied) sits in the workspace root: `remove` needs an approval channel that this session does not have, so it was kept.\n"
