          "kind": "finished",
          "message": "## Done — a real INI parser for this repo's dialect\n\n`moon test` (cold build after `moon clean`): **37 tests, 37 passed, 0 failed**; `moon check`: **0 errors**. No warnings come from any file I wrote (the three remaining ones are the pre-existing warnings in `ini_spec.mbt`'s `derive`, `ini_pub_test.mbt`'s unqualified `Doc`, and `moon.pkg`'s unused `core/test` import — all in files I must not modify).\n\n### Files\n\n| File | Lines | Role |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| `line_source.mbt` | 105 | splits input into physical lines (LF / CRLF, trailing blanks dropped) and the `priv struct LineSource` cursor with continuation lookahead |\n| `char_utils.mbt` | 69 | `is_blank`, `is_control`, `skip_blanks`, `skip_blanks_back`, `copy_range`, `text_of` |\n| `value_parser.mbt` | 219 | quoted values (per-carrier escapes, same-line closing, tail check) and unquoted values (inline comment → continuation → trim → escape decode) |\n| `document_parser.mbt` | 150 | `pub fn parse`: line classification, section headers, entries, `Doc` assembly |\n| `printer.mbt` | 88 | `pub fn print`: global entries first, then per section; every value double-quoted and escaped |\n| `ini_parse_test.mbt` | 367 | 25 added black-box tests derived from `specs/ini.md` |\n| `README.md` | 241 | overview, architecture, algorithms, escape/continuation tables, usage, testing, design decisions |\n\n`ini_spec.mbt`, `ini_qc.mbt`, `ini_pub_test.mbt` and `specs/` are byte-identical to the originals (`moon fmt` rewrote `ini_spec.mbt`'s `derive` once; I restored it and verified all 94 lines).\n\n### Key implementation decisions\n\n- **Raw text before escapes.** Continuation counts the trailing-backslash *run* on the raw line: odd → marker removed and next line appended directly; even → escaped literals. That is the only way `k=a\\` and `k=a\\\\` stay distinguishable.\n- **Comment before join.** Inline `;`/`#` (only after a blank) is stripped on the line that carries it, so a continuation line's `=`, `:`, quotes and comment markers remain value text — verified by a test where `nextkey=value` and ` ; #` are joined into one value.\n- **Trim then decode** for unquoted values, which keeps `a \\` + `b` → `a b` and leaves `\\t` escapes intact at value ends.\n- **Strict section syntax**: exactly `[name]` (nothing after `]`), no nested brackets, non-empty trimmed name, one wrapping quote pair stripped (`[\"a b\"]` → `a b`, `[remote \"origin\"]` unchanged).\n- **LF/CRLF only**: split at LF, drop the CR of CRLF; a lone CR is data (control char in a key → rejected).\n- **Printing** uses double quotes for every value with exactly the escapes that carrier decodes, plus extra quotes around section names that would otherwise be trimmed or lose a quote pair, so `parse(print(doc)) == doc` holds — exercised by 3 300 generated documents (300 in the suite, 3 000 in a temporary stress run) and a 3 000-string no-panic fuzz.\n\n### Caveat\n\nA temporary `probe/` program was used to eyeball edge cases; its files are deleted, but a stale `probe/pkg.generated.mbti` (13 lines, no package manifest, no sources) could not be deleted — the `remove` tool requires approval for it and this session has no approval channel. Moon ignores directories without `moon.pkg`, which the clean rebuild confirmed.\n"
